    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0168" n="156" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg156"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/2628</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Brazilian Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Aranha</hi>)<anchor
                        n="78" xml:id="d150-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1942</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-11-09">November 9, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    note of Your Excellency of October 8, 1943, number DEC/373/832.1 (42)
                        (22)<anchor n="76" xml:id="d150-f2"/> attaching a Memorandum<anchor n="79"
                        xml:id="d150-f3"/> proposing the partial modification of the existing
                    procedure now being followed by the Carteira de Exportação <pb facs="0169"
                        n="157" xml:id="pg157"/> e Importação of the Bank of Brazil, with the
                    collaboration of my Embassy, in handling Preference Requests for the importation
                    of materials from or via the United States.</p>
                <p>The Memorandum described above was referred to my Government which has offered
                    certain suggestions in view of existing conditions. I, therefore, now have the
                    honor to transmit for Your Excellency’s kind consideration a new Memorandum on
                    the subject, on which representatives of the Carteira, my Embassy and the
                    Commercial Counselor of Your Excellency’s Embassy in Washington are in
                    agreement.</p>
                <p>I submit this having in mind the provisions of Your Excellency’s note of October
                    8, referred to previously.</p>


                <xi:include href="d150-a1.xml" xpointer="d150-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d150-f1" n="78" type="source" xml:id="d150-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Ambassador in his despatch No. 13671,
                    December 2; received December 10. This supplementary agreement by an exchange of
                    notes was authorized in Department’s telegram No. 4145, November 6, midnight
                    (832.24/2501).</p>
            </note>
